  "output": {
    "svg": "architecture.svg",
    "medium": "documentation and notebook",
    "alt_text": "A researcher agent produces a peer message whose prose remains untrusted. A trusted gateway authenticates the workload edge and checks tenant, type, source registry, replay, and lifetime before issuing an integrity-bound envelope containing source references, taint labels, and allowed uses. A writer receives minimized admitted context, while a transformation gate requires unchanged security metadata on the derived artifact. A separate authorizer validates the current actor, target, policy, artifact, and taint before one narrow idempotent effect. Every stage emits a redacted receipt without raw content or credentials."
  },
